            <ArticleTitle>Transesophageal echocardiographic demonstration of right coronary artery-to-coronary sinus fistula in a heart transplant recipient.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>449-52</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A fistula between the distal right coronary artery and coronary sinus was detected by transesophageal echocardiography in a heart transplant recipient. Cineangiograms confirmed this finding to be new since the time of angiography one year earlier. Although coronary artery-to-right ventricular fistulas are not an uncommon complication of endomyocardial biopsy, the echocardiographic findings of a fistula involving the coronary sinus have not been previously described.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
